1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,045
Everything
in orange

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,868
was underwater
in 2000.

3
00:00:03,019 --> 00:00:03,866
Lake Mead.

4
00:00:03,982 --> 00:00:05,886
America's largest
reservoir.

5
00:00:06,211 --> 00:00:07,233
Watch it drain.

6
00:00:07,558 --> 00:00:09,253
Since 2000,
its water level

7
00:00:09,311 --> 00:00:11,447
has dropped
about 160 feet.

8
00:00:11,726 --> 00:00:13,142
Its northern
arm pulled

9
00:00:13,189 --> 00:00:14,791
back
about nine miles.

10
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,603
About half
of its surface water

11
00:00:16,672 --> 00:00:17,404
is gone.

12
00:00:17,729 --> 00:00:20,341
In 2022, it hit
its lowest

13
00:00:20,422 --> 00:00:21,607
level since
it was first

14
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,511
filled
in the 1930s.

15
00:00:23,894 --> 00:00:25,635
Why?
A long drought

16
00:00:25,682 --> 00:00:26,924
on the Colorado
River.

17
00:00:27,203 --> 00:00:29,455
Year after year,
more water left

18
00:00:29,501 --> 00:00:30,964
the lake
than flowed in.

19
00:00:31,289 --> 00:00:33,147
That river system
supplies water

20
00:00:33,217 --> 00:00:35,237
to about 40
million people.

21
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:38,116
Then,
in August 2026,

22
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:40,125
Lake Mead broke
that record.

23
00:00:40,728 --> 00:00:41,611
Lower than ever.

24
00:00:42,121 --> 00:00:43,015
That white line

25
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,676
is where the water
used to be.
